<title>FRANCE: Dasa wins 30 mln DM space contract.</title>
<headline>Dasa wins 30 mln DM space contract.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Daimler-Benz Aerospace AG said on Friday it won a 30 million mark contract to build system controls for Europe's Ariane 5 rocket.</p>
<p>Dasa, a unit of car maker Daimler-Benz AG, would build 14 systems for Mantra Marconi Space (MMS), a unit of France's Lagardere SA group. The systems control the Ariane 5's path during ascent and orbit.</p>
<p>The contract was announced at the Paris air show.</p>
<p>Dasa, whose first-quarter sales rose 39 percent to 3.9 billion marks, recently agreed to combine its space activities with MMS. It also agreed to sell Lagardere a 30 percent share in its LFK GmbH missile guidance systems subsidiary.</p>
<p>-- Neal Boudette, Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
